<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document>
<name>Line 5 tenders: route and chainage (Oct 2026)</name>
<description>Line 5 past Dhamankar Naka as MMRDA's civil tenders of Oct 2026 draw it (CA-317, CA-318, CA-314). The route is traced from the key plan in the tender drawings (MMRDA-MML-05-MTR-GAD-TD-1000, CA-314 Volume V), placed on the map by fitting its Line 12 to MMRDA's Line 12 file and its route to the six stations whose coordinates the CA-317 and CA-318 plan sheets print (UTM 43N, WGS84). Those six stations are within 6 m of the traced line and within 6 m of the main road in OpenStreetMap. Other stations are placed by their tender chainage along the line (good to about 50 m). Built by scripts/line5-tenders/assemble.py. Chainage ticks every 100 m, labelled every 500 m, in the tender notation km+m. Main line chainage has the same zero as the Phase 1 environmental report; spur chainage is the spur's own (tender US chainage minus 26,177). Green stations: coordinates printed in the tender. Yellow: placed by chainage, good to about 50 m. Mumbai Metro Tracker, mumbaimetrotracker.com. Route traced from MMRDA's drawings; roads from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</description>
